    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        705.3422241210938,
        527.112548828125,
        719.7852172851562
      ],
      "text": "TB remains the primary cause of AIDS-related morbidity and mortality worldwide, despite impressive",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.995498657226562,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        718.542236328125,
        527.4487915039062,
        732.9852294921875
      ],
      "text": "scale up of antiretroviral treatment (ART). In 2019, TB was associated with an estimated 208 000 (30%)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.979731559753418,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        728.9481811523438,
        524.5531005859375,
        746.1851806640625
      ],
      "text": "(1) AIDS-related deaths  . Global estimates show a 44% gap in case detection among people with HIV-",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.991347312927246,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        742.148193359375,
        527.3988037109375,
        759.3851928710938
      ],
      "text": "(1) associated TB  . A systematic review of postmortem studies of global AIDS-related deaths in adults",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        758.1422119140625,
        527.50732421875,
        772.585205078125
      ],
      "text": "found TB to be the primary cause of death in 37.2% of cases (95% CI: 25.7–48.7). TB was undiagnosed",
